for MeiraGTx ADS Injector

















 
1.0	PURPOSE
This protocol defines the methods and materials needed to verify the effectiveness of the shipping configuration for the MeiraGTx Acute Delivery System (ADS) Injector within an ISTA 3A shipping model.
2.0	SCOPE
This protocol solely applies to the MeiraGTx ADS Injector and the provided Packaged Assembly. The scope is limited to the verification of the Packaged Assembly in providing adequate protection to the ADS Injector during transit testing, per ISTA 3A, while also satisfying part of the Design Input Requirements specified in PPC-0961-20000 and listed in Table 1. A qualified third-party, Unified2 Global Packaging Group, provides the Carton Packaged Assembly and performs the transit test. Further functional evaluation of the packaging is conducted by NextPhase Medical Devices LLC (NXP).
Table 1: Design Inputs
Requirement ID #	Requirement
ID-5-001	The Injector packaging shall pass evaluation per ISTA 3A test methods.
ID-5-002	The Injector shall pass critical functional requirements after ISTA 3A conditioning.
3.0	BACKGROUND
The MeiraGTx ADS Injector is an infusion pump intended for the direct accurate delivery of the AAV-GAD gene therapy drug to brain parenchyma. The system shall be used by physicians and operating room nurses familiar with neurosurgery within post-operative recovery rooms, as well as inside and outside the sterile field in the operating room of professional healthcare facilities that are familiar with neurosurgery.

NextPhase Medical Devices is an FDA registered and EN ISO 13485:2016 certified organization with significant expertise in medical device design, verification and validation, and manufacturing.

The design of the study is appropriate because ISTA 3A is an internationally recognized test method used to evaluate packaging commonly distributed as individual packages, either by air or ground, such as the one designed for the MeiraGTx ADS Injector.
