Record the Identification number and calibration due date of all equipment used in this protocol in Appendix 1 Calibration sheet. If a piece of equipment is not calibrated because the output is measured by another calibrated equipment, record the equipment that monitors the output.
12.0	TEST PROCEDURE
12.1	Setup
12.1.1	Obtain (1) DWG-0961-20031, MeiraGTx ADS Injector, from the DV Build.
12.1.2	Verify test article meets the requirements of TM-0961-20000 and retain a copy of the completed functional test data sheet(s) per TM-0961-20000, for inclusion in the test report upon completion.
12.1.3	Package the test articles according to MP-0961-20000.
12.1.3.1	Corrugated board shipping boxes are to be visually inspected for damage prior to packing the test articles. All observations are to be recorded in Appendix 2.
12.1.3.2	Inspect interior foam supports for any damage prior to packing the ADS Injector. All observations are to be recorded in Attachment 2.
12.1.3.3	Inspect additional items included within the packaging per MP-0961-20000 (AC Power Cord, Power Adapter, IFU). All observations are to be recorded in Attachment 2.
12.1.3.4	Any damage or abnormalities found during visual inspections should be photographed and documented in the report.
12.1.4	Verify the items contained within the package reside in their proper position, with no items missing. Record any findings in Appendix 2.
12.1.5	Produce a bar code on a blank shipper label.
NOTE: The information on the label can be for any product.
12.1.6	Attach the label to the shipping box.
12.1.7	Verify the size and weight of the shipping box.
12.1.8	Verify the label(s) are adhered to the cardboard shipping box.
12.1.9	Verify label(s) are legible.
12.1.10	Verify the bar code(s) are scannable.
12.1.11	Submit the test article to the 3rd party test service for testing.
12.1.12	3rd party test service will verify the size and weight of the shipping box. 
12.2	Procedure – ISTA conditioning & testing
NOTE: These steps to be performed by 3rd party test house. Test house must document actual conditions in their report.
12.2.1	Verify size and weight of the test article.
12.2.2	Store test article at ambient temperature for a minimum of 6 hours.
•	Ambient Temperature = 23 °C ± 2 °C (73 °F ± 4 °F)
•	Ambient Relative Humidity (RH) = 50% RH ± 5%
12.2.3	Conduct ISTA 3A testing using the information from Step 10.1 (size and weight) and the tests specified for STANDARD/SMALL packaged-products.
12.2.4	Sign and date any data sheets.
12.2.5	Provide a report containing the details of the testing.
12.3	procedure – post-test inspection and function verification
	NOTE: Record all observations and comments on the data sheet.
12.3.1	Shipping Box Inspection
12.3.1.1	Inspect shipping box for damage prior to un-packing the ADS Injector. All abnormalities are to be recorded in Appendix 3.
12.3.1.2	Any damage or abnormalities found during visual inspection should be photographed and documented in the report.
12.3.2	Label Inspection
12.3.2.1	Examine the labels on the shipping box.
12.3.2.2	Verify that the labels are legible.
12.3.2.3	Verify that any bar codes are scannable.
12.3.2.4	Verify that labels are adhered to the shipper box.
12.3.2.5	Record findings in Appendix 3.
12.3.3	Post-Test Functional Device Verification
12.3.3.1	Verify the items contained within the shipping box reside in their proper position, with no items missing. Record findings in Appendix 3. 
12.3.3.2	Un-pack the items and verify that they are free from visible damage. All damage or abnormalities are to be recorded in Appendix 3.
12.3.3.3	Any damage or abnormalities found during visual inspection should be photographed and documented in the report.
12.3.3.4	Use the ADS Injector Assembly to perform the EOL functional test per TM-0961-20000.
12.3.3.5	The ability to perform the EOL functional test per TM-0961-20000 using the ADS Injector test article satisfies the functional test requirement. Document results in Appendix 3.
